# Copy to .env locally if desired. Never commit a real value.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=YOUR_OPENROUTER_API_KEY
TYPESAFE_API_KEY=YOUR_TYPESAFE_API_KEY
# openrouter, typesafe, typesafe_then_openrouter, openrouter_then_typesafe,
# laya, or a local first chain: laya_then_typesafe, laya_then_openrouter,
# laya_then_typesafe_openrouter, laya_then_openrouter_typesafe.
# The DOGA selector names laya_local and laya_with_jev_fallback are also accepted:
# laya_local is laya, and laya_with_jev_fallback is laya_then_openrouter_typesafe,
# which tries laya, then openrouter, then typesafe.
# The four hosted modes run Jev over a hosted key. `laya` runs Laya locally with no
# key and no hosted hop. A `laya_then_*` mode answers locally first and falls
# through to the hosted provider(s) it names, so a failed local attempt sends the
# case state to that hosted API; the key for every named provider is required, and
# a missing one stops the mode at selection. After three consecutive local failures
# in one process the fallback stops and the local error is raised instead, until a
# local answer succeeds again.
JEV_PROVIDER_MODE=openrouter
# The local hop. Read by `laya` and by every `laya_then_*` mode.
JEV_LAYA_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8123
JEV_LAYA_ENDPOINT_PATH=/v1/systemone
JEV_LAYA_MODEL=english
# Only for a laya-serve started with its own bearer check. Leave unset otherwise.
# LAYA_API_KEY=YOUR_LAYA_SERVER_TOKEN
JEV_HOME=$HOME/.jev
